            <ArticleTitle>[A diagnostic trap simulating pulmonary embolism].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>420-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pulmonary embolism is one of the differential diagnoses of &quot;acute chest&quot; syndromes. We report a clinical case of contained rupture of ascending aortic aneurysm with pulmonary arteries compression, which was presented as pulmonary embolism, and we well review the literature data of this diagnostic trap.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
